 "comment": "I am very confident in the final count of 456 oat kernels. The kernels were arranged in a horseshoe/arch pattern with a few stray kernels near the bottom. The main challenge was the dense packing along the arch where narrow oat kernels lay side-by-side within a third of a kernel length (approx. 25 px) of each other; this caused the automatic duplicate-rejection radius to initially reject valid adjacent kernels, which required re-viewing the marked regions and using force=true to place marks on closely packed neighbours. Conversely, because oat kernels are elongated relative to their width, marking near opposite ends of a kernel across overlapping view seams occasionally bypassed the duplicate radius and required manual removal upon re-inspection. Spreading the kernels slightly further apart on the sheet or using an elliptical/smaller duplicate-check radius for elongated grains like oats would make counting even smoother.",
